    12	
    13	Finance QA traced rerun drift to parsers that latched onto the wrong ledger
    14	slice. For extractor output, treat only the markdown section whose heading
    15	line is exactly `## Transaction Ledger` as authoritative. The archive also
    16	contains a working-copy ledger and prose that mentions ledger headings; those
    17	are investigative context only.
    18	
    19	Ignore any ledger block that includes a line `provisional: true` (case
    20	insensitive). When the same transaction id appears in multiple non-provisional
    21	ledger blocks, the last such block in file order is the base row for that id.
    22	
    23	Locate section boundaries with regular expressions anchored to whole heading
    24	lines at line start. Do not locate sections with indexOf or substring search.
    25	
    26	## Investigation Brief 01 — Ledger Sourcing — supporting chronology
    27	
    28	Audit technologist T. Singh replayed FY24 mailbox snapshots and showed how inventory obsolescence reserve threads arrived out of order relative to correction notices, surfacing effective-date mismatch on four high-balance rows.
    29	
    30	Controller staff described inventory obsolescence reserve as a secondary driver of mailbox ingestion lag while rebuilding the October count close calendar. They emphasized that decoy ledger headings in draft appendices must be ignored.
    31	
    32	Treasury liaison E. Novak explained that inventory obsolescence reserve related wires were paused during October count, delaying compliance responses and amplifying mailbox ingestion lag on rejected rows.
    33	
    34	Internal audit follow-up #145 tracked how inventory obsolescence reserve exceptions were closed without matching policy waiver paperwork, a separate issue from extractor merge ordering.
    35	
    36	Stakeholder workshop #818 on inventory obsolescence reserve produced conflicting recollections about which correction notice superseded an earlier owner change; Brief 04 governs that precedence for automated output.
    37	
    38	Platform engineer J. Huang noted that inventory obsolescence reserve webhook retries duplicated compliance messages in the investigative export, requiring deduplication by subject and sent timestamp during human review.
    39	
    40	Data governance WP-3763 catalogs legacy operations finance folders still containing inventory obsolescence reserve spreadsheets. Those folders are evidentiary only; extractor output must come from canonical structured sections.
    41	
    42	SOX testing team WP-6621 linked policy waiver omission on inventory obsolescence reserve to a manual override logged at 02:14 local time between two automated correction imports.
    43	
    44	Peer review #417 of operations finance sampling found 14 mislinked emails on inventory obsolescence reserve. None of the mislinked messages originated from compliance addresses, supporting Brief 02 sender restrictions.
    45	
    46	Tax counsel flagged inventory obsolescence reserve restatement risk during October count close, unrelated to extractor precedence but relevant to why the archive retains full correspondence.
    47	
    48	Interview #743 with operations finance counsel captured how inventory obsolescence reserve correspondence referenced amounts near $45,275 without matching ledger rows. Investigators preserved the thread because hold flag suppression can change downstream exception coding.
    49	
    50	Vendor management L. Bergstrom described inventory obsolescence reserve onboarding delays that pushed compliance responses past ledger dates on several rejected rows during October count.
    51	
    52	Follow-up #384 confirmed that operations finance routed inventory obsolescence reserve statements through a shared inbox with 5 delegates. Investigators flagged ledger slice confusion as the likely root cause of inconsistent status columns.
    53	
    54	Fixed-assets specialist A. Ndiaye argued that inventory obsolescence reserve capitalization memos should not alter ledger status; investigators agreed while noting those memos still inform exception coding narratives.
    55	
    56	External advisors reviewing inventory obsolescence reserve during October count asked for a machine-readable trace explaining why rejected rows received hold flags. The archive preserves narrative chronology even though only structured tail sections are authoritative.
    57	
    58	Lead reviewer R. Okonkwo opened working paper WP-9944 after operations finance reported that inventory obsolescence reserve distorted the October count reconciliation. The team reconstructed mailbox ordering and found correction batch ordering affecting at least 17 transaction threads.
    59	
    60	Quality review #538 sampled 9 inventory obsolescence reserve tickets and found correction batch ordering whenever provisional ledger rows were not filtered before merge.
    61	
    62	In October count, operations finance migrated inventory obsolescence reserve workflows to a new ticketing tool. Migration cutover introduced effective-date mismatch, which did not reproduce once ledger sourcing rules from Brief 01 were applied manually.
    63	
    64	Draft sidebar (non-authoritative): some prototype tooling compared compliance mail timestamps against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. Brief 09 later in this archive supersedes that draft practice for production reconciliation.
    65	
    66	Risk assessment WP-5894 links inventory obsolescence reserve to control gaps in mail ingestion for operations finance. The assessment explicitly warns against treating alternate ledger headings or appendix commentary as transaction sources.
    67	
    68	Counsel memo WP-4822 advises retaining full inventory obsolescence reserve threads because litigation hold scope may extend beyond the transactions named in formal notices.
    69	
    70	Regional lead S. Patel hosted a readout on inventory obsolescence reserve where finance controllers disputed whether unsigned meeting notes should override ledger owners; investigators cited Brief 05 during the session.
    71	
    72	Privacy review #137 redacted personal data from inventory obsolescence reserve threads but retained transaction identifiers needed for reconciliation testing.
