    26	## Investigation Brief 01 — Ledger Sourcing — supporting chronology
    27	
    28	Audit technologist T. Singh replayed FY24 mailbox snapshots and showed how inventory obsolescence reserve threads arrived out of order relative to correction notices, surfacing effective-date mismatch on four high-balance rows.
    29	
    30	Controller staff described inventory obsolescence reserve as a secondary driver of mailbox ingestion lag while rebuilding the October count close calendar. They emphasized that decoy ledger headings in draft appendices must be ignored.
    31	
    32	Treasury liaison E. Novak explained that inventory obsolescence reserve related wires were paused during October count, delaying compliance responses and amplifying mailbox ingestion lag on rejected rows.
    33	
    34	Internal audit follow-up #145 tracked how inventory obsolescence reserve exceptions were closed without matching policy waiver paperwork, a separate issue from extractor merge ordering.
    35	
    36	Stakeholder workshop #818 on inventory obsolescence reserve produced conflicting recollections about which correction notice superseded an earlier owner change; Brief 04 governs that precedence for automated output.
