   856	## Investigation Brief 06 — Effective Dates on Output
   857	
   858	Auditors compared effective_date columns to correction paperwork. Start from the
   859	ledger `date` field (YYYY-MM-DD on output). When a winning correction notice
   860	sets field `date` or `status`, use that notice's `effective` date as
   861	`effective_date` only if that correction modified status or date; otherwise
   862	keep the ledger date. `amount_usd` is numeric from the ledger with two decimal
   863	places in CSV and as a JSON number.
   864	
